    rt_call_site_ratchet_regression_2026-09-05, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: gate had drifted to forbidden=6926 over baseline=6290 (committed content, reproduced at HEAD). Classified all 156 non-allowlisted offender files in the two named domain trees against the allowlist criterion: 98 files/697 sites are legitimate providers (io ABI wrapper leaves, Windows/Linux/SOSIX/Darwin native owners, SIMD/SDL/winit/font vendor ABI, SPipe BDD rt_bdd_*, coverage/fork/DAP/XRay seams, rt_db C-engine bindings, noalloc freestanding redeclarations) - allowlisted with owner notes per convention in scripts/check/no_direct_rt_allowlist.txt (+118 lines) plus the required record doc/08_tracking/rt_boundary/two_domain_tree_provider_tranche_2026-11-27.md. 58 files/283 sites remain forbidden as real regressions with reroute prescriptions recorded (io_runtime.spl 52, observer_native_channel_v1.spl 50, interpreter_backend.spl 17, storage_roots/publisher.spl 16 et al). After: PASS (src=6229, forbidden=6229 within baseline 6290, headroom 61) + --selftest-only PASS 24 fixtures. Baseline file deliberately untouched (doc forbids re-baselining); the perf_checklists_spec oracle stays RED by design per the doc. Scanner false-positive on rt_criticality_validation.spl (211, rt_*-named pure predicates) documented as out of scope. close_evidence reproducer=doc/08_tracking/rt_boundary/two_domain_tree_provider_tranche_2026-11-27.md prevention=scripts/check/no_direct_rt_allowlist.txt"

